# Showcase

<Admonition type="tip" title="Seen one we can't do?">

If you come across a cropper on the web that you think this library can't reproduce, [open an issue](https://github.com/jakeklassen/svelte-advanced-cropper/issues) and describe it. Those cases are the best test of the API.

</Admonition>

This page rebuilds croppers from well-known sites. They are ordinary demos built from the public components and the `advanced-cropper` core, so each one shows how far you can take the library without touching its internals. Open "Show code" under a demo to read every file it uses.

## Telegram

A take on the photo cropper in Telegram's mobile app. The stencil can't be dragged: you resize it from its corners, and when you let go it grows back to fill the space while the image zooms to match. Below the image, a dial rotates it in fine steps up to 45° either way, the side buttons turn it by quarters, and the flip buttons stay true to the screen even after a quarter turn.

The behaviour comes from the core's `advanced-cropper/showcase/mobile` module (`stencilConstraints`, `fitStencilToImage`, `zoomStencil`, `defaultSize`, `transformImage` and `resizeCoordinates`), plugged into a regular `Cropper` through its settings and algorithm props. The toolbar is a custom `wrapperComponent`, the dial is built on `DraggableArea`, and the corners theme is applied to this cropper only.

<Example source={telegramShowcaseSource} title="TelegramShowcase" files={{ 'TelegramCropper.svelte': telegramCropperSource, 'CropperWrapper.svelte': telegramWrapperSource, 'Navigation.svelte': telegramNavigationSource, 'RotateComponent.svelte': telegramRotateSource, 'types.ts': telegramTypesSource }}>
	<TelegramShowcase />
</Example>

<Admonition type="info" title="Using it in your app">

The React family publishes this cropper as a separate package, [react-mobile-cropper](https://github.com/advanced-cropper/react-mobile-cropper). There is no Svelte package for it yet, but the demo is self-contained: copy its files into your project and adjust them as you like.

</Admonition>

## Twitter

A take on the avatar cropper from Twitter. The square stencil is fixed in the middle and the image moves and zooms beneath it, with a slider underneath to control the zoom. It is a `FixedCropper` with a custom wrapper, and the slider position comes from the core's `absolute-zoom` extension (`getAbsoluteZoom` and `getZoomFactor`).

<Example source={twitterShowcaseSource} title="TwitterShowcase" files={{ 'TwitterCropper.svelte': twitterCropperSource, 'Wrapper.svelte': twitterWrapperSource, 'Navigation.svelte': twitterNavigationSource, 'Slider.svelte': sliderSource }}>
	<TwitterShowcase />
</Example>
